<title>FRANCE: BNP holds 1.4 pct of Suez voting rights.</title>
<headline>BNP holds 1.4 pct of Suez voting rights.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Nationale de Paris (BNP) holds 1.42 percent of the voting rights in Compagnie de Suez, bourse regulator CMF (Conseil des marches financiers) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Last week the bank said it sold 3.05 percent of its capital in Suez. Rumours circulated in the markets that Belgian businessman Albert Frere's Groupe Bruxelles Lambert (GBL) was the buyer.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
